From 3c44336aa581c65dab685ff2df8e5cb2502d675c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Neil G. Brookins" <31250635+neilbrookins@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:52:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] html: fit again after the renderer changes

ttyd fits the terminal once in open(), with xterm.js's DOM renderer.
The rendererType preference (WebGL by default) arrives afterwards, and
the new renderer measures character cells differently, but nothing fits
again until a window resize: the terminal keeps the columns of the first
fit (150 instead of 167 at 1200x900 in Chrome), and programs are told
that size, so lines stop short of the right edge.

Fit once more after the new renderer has drawn. A fit straight after
loadAddon() is not enough: the renderer measures its cells when it
draws.

Fixes #1534

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 html/src/components/terminal/xterm/index.ts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/html/src/components/terminal/xterm/index.ts b/html/src/components/terminal/xterm/index.ts
index b332154..6de46a0 100644
--- a/html/src/components/terminal/xterm/index.ts
+++ b/html/src/components/terminal/xterm/index.ts
@@ -531,5 +531,13 @@ export class Xterm {
             default:
                 break;
         }
+
+        // The new renderer may measure character cells differently from the one the
+        // terminal was fitted with, so fit again once it has drawn; otherwise the
+        // terminal keeps too few (or too many) columns until the window is resized.
+        const disposable = terminal.onRender(() => {
+            disposable.dispose();
+            this.fitAddon.fit();
+        });
     }
 }
